# Terraform Module: S3 + RDS + IAM

A reusable Terraform module provisioning an encrypted, versioned S3 bucket, a hardened RDS PostgreSQL instance, and a least-privilege IAM role for service accounts (IRSA-compatible). Environment separation via `*.tfvars` + separate backend state keys.

---

## Repository layout

```
.
├── modules/
│   └── app-platform/
│       ├── versions.tf
│       ├── variables.tf
│       ├── locals.tf
│       ├── s3.tf
│       ├── kms.tf
│       ├── rds.tf
│       ├── iam.tf
│       ├── secrets.tf
│       └── outputs.tf
├── envs/
│   ├── dev/
│   │   ├── backend.tf
│   │   ├── main.tf
│   │   ├── providers.tf
│   │   ├── outputs.tf
│   │   └── dev.tfvars
│   └── prod/
│       ├── backend.tf
│       ├── main.tf
│       ├── providers.tf
│       ├── outputs.tf
│       └── prod.tfvars
├── Makefile
└── README.md
```

---

## `modules/app-platform/versions.tf`

```hcl
terraform {
  required_version = ">= 1.6.0"

  required_providers {
    aws = {
      source                = "hashicorp/aws"
      version               = "~> 5.40"
      configuration_aliases = [aws.replica]
    }
    random = {
      source  = "hashicorp/random"
      version = "~> 3.6"
    }
  }
}
```

> The `aws.replica` alias is always required by the module, but the replication
> resources are only created when `enable_replication = true`. Callers that do
> not need replication can pass the same provider twice.

